abstract: "Historical monetary and economic data spanning twenty centuries (1 CE–present), compiled from 27 public sources with a reproducible build pipeline: exchange rates (236 countries, chain-linked across redenominations), gold, silver, interest rates, CPI, GDP per capita, commodity prices, real wages, sovereign debt, regime classifications, and real effective exchange rates. The MIT license covers the code; each source's data keeps its own terms (see DATA_CARD.md)."
